<title>USA: U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - June 16.</title>
<headline>U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - June 16.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>-- Northwest Airlines Corp is close to an agreement with Airbus Industrie to order 50 jetliners worth $2 billion, the Wall Street Journal reported.</p>
<p>-- International Business Machines Corp plans to introduce a new line of data-storage products that would allow computers using diferent operating systems to have access to a single source of data, according to the New York Times.</p>
<p>-- Fila Holdings SpA said on Friday it expects earnings for the second quarter to be in the range of $0.53 per share and $0.60 per share, below the analysts' consensus estimate of $0.88 per share.</p>
</text>
